             84  ************************************************************
             85  *  MODIFICATIONS DONE SINCE FIRST OPERATIONAL              *
             86  *                                                          *
             87  * BREAKPOINT HANDLER CHANGED SO AS NOT TO DELETE B.P.'S    *
             88  *   WHEN THEY ARE 'HIT', ALSO CHANGED SO AS NOT TO CLEAR   *
             89  *   BREAKPOINTS ON SYSTEM RESET.                           *
             90  * OUTPUT ROUTINE: ESCAPE DETECT WRITTEN IN, SO AS TO GIVE  *
             91  *  RETURN TO COMMAND SCANNER WHEN ESCAPE IS PRESSED        *
             92  * ASSEMBLER AND DISASSEMBLER RE-WRITTEN SO AS TO USE       *
             93  *  COMBINED TEXT/DATA TABLES.                              *
             94  * NEGATIVE FIND ROUTINE ADDED                              *
             95  * SINGLE STEP TO VALUE ADDED                               *
             96  * MID, AO, & UNDEFINED XOP HANDLERS ADDED.                 *
             97  * PRINT FORMAT IN 'R' & 'M' COMMANDS ALTERED SO AS TO USE  *
             98  *  40 CHARACTER VDU'S                                      *
             99  * BREAKPOINT HANDLING CHANGED SO AS TO REMOVE BPTS FROM    *
            100  * USER RAM IN THE MONTOP. ALSO CHANGED SO THAT A SINGLE    *
            101  * STEP IS EXECUTED BEFORE THE BPTS ARE SET.                *
            102  * SINGLE STEP ROUTINES RE-WRITTEN SO AS TO USE LESS CODE   *
            103  * USER VECTOR FOR BREAKPOINT ZERO INTRODUCED.              *
            104  * PRINT FORMAT FOR 'F' & 'N' COMMANDS CHANGED              *
            105  * SINGLE STEP/TRACE CHANGED SO AS NOT TO OUTPUT IN XOP'S   *
            106  ************************************************************
